    {
      "id": "fz-qJjtZaGD1-oX0KAXAM",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4292.744767658471,
      "y": 1557.9378534065277,
      "width": 333.39050955182347,
      "height": 250,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#b2f2bb",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0H",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 67331424,
      "version": 464,
      "versionNonce": 1197489312,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "mL4w6r0xuUxlBBt5NHhFP",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1789447433630,
      "created": 1789447433617,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Relocatability: A program can be\ncompiled assuming its code starts\nat address 0. When loaded into\nphysical RAM at address 80000,\nan Address Translation Unit\n(ATU) or loader adds a base\noffset (80000) to every logical\nreference without changing the\noriginal binary image\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Relocatability: A program can be compiled assuming its code starts at address 0. When loaded into physical RAM at address 80000, an Address Translation Unit (ATU) or loader adds a base offset (80000) to every logical reference without changing the original binary image\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "3ywowYRrV5NX8Pk1aYzjt",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4651.498960018469,
      "y": 1644.9317226148703,
      "width": 261.7036007650595,
      "height": 275,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#b2f2bb",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0I",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1831844192,
      "version": 465,
      "versionNonce": 189226336,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "3-9XwCZeBGYNZsULB0Zmi",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1789447433630,
      "created": 1789447433617,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Program Isolation &\nProtection: The operating\nsystem enforces memory\nboundaries on logical\naddress ranges. If a\nprocess attempts to\ngenerate a logical address\noutside its allocated\nrange, the hardware MMU\ntriggers a segmentation\nfault / trap",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Program Isolation & Protection: The operating system enforces memory boundaries on logical address ranges. If a process attempts to generate a logical address outside its allocated range, the hardware MMU triggers a segmentation fault / trap",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "FJd084iPGg0RR_M8v9wPl",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4955.175016378373,
      "y": 1597.9314246613026,
      "width": 249.16944636700418,
      "height": 175,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#b2f2bb",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0J",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 363957600,
      "version": 721,
      "versionNonce": 896510112,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "dUAlXCkAZZnij1QSRRRPQ",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1789447433630,
      "created": 1789447433617,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Virtual Memory: Enables a\nprogram's logical address\nspace to be significantly\nlarger than physical RAM\nby storing unreferenced\nmemory pages on\nsecondary disk storage",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Virtual Memory: Enables a program's logical address space to be significantly larger than physical RAM by storing unreferenced memory pages on secondary disk storage",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
