      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1789618550591,
      "created": 1789618549302,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "+-------------------+----------------------------------------+----------------------------------------+\n| Aspect            | Variant I                              | Variant II                             |\n+-------------------+----------------------------------------+----------------------------------------+\n| Operand           | Memory operands are fully converted    | Memory operands are kept as raw        |\n| Representation    | into tuple descriptors (S, #n),        | source strings (AREG, A) and processed |\n|                   | (L, #m), (C, val) during Pass 1        | in Pass 2                              |\n+-------------------+----------------------------------------+----------------------------------------+\n| Work Division     | Pass 1 performs heavy work;            | Work is balanced evenly between        |\n|                   | Pass 2 becomes trivial and fast        | Pass 1 and Pass 2                      |\n+-------------------+----------------------------------------+----------------------------------------+\n| Memory Efficiency | Highly compact IC file. However,       | IC file is less compact, but overall   |\n|                   | Pass 1 code size is much larger        | assembler memory is lower because      |\n|                   | than Pass 2                            | code sizes are comparable              |\n+-------------------+----------------------------------------+----------------------------------------+\n| Expression        | Complex for expressions like           | Extremely clean for expressions—leaves |\n| Support           | A+5 into (S, 01)+5                     | A+5 in source string form for Pass 2   |\n+-------------------+----------------------------------------+----------------------------------------+",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "+-------------------+----------------------------------------+----------------------------------------+\n| Aspect            | Variant I                              | Variant II                             |\n+-------------------+----------------------------------------+----------------------------------------+\n| Operand           | Memory operands are fully converted    | Memory operands are kept as raw        |\n| Representation    | into tuple descriptors (S, #n),        | source strings (AREG, A) and processed |\n|                   | (L, #m), (C, val) during Pass 1        | in Pass 2                              |\n+-------------------+----------------------------------------+----------------------------------------+\n| Work Division     | Pass 1 performs heavy work;            | Work is balanced evenly between        |\n|                   | Pass 2 becomes trivial and fast        | Pass 1 and Pass 2                      |\n+-------------------+----------------------------------------+----------------------------------------+\n| Memory Efficiency | Highly compact IC file. However,       | IC file is less compact, but overall   |\n|                   | Pass 1 code size is much larger        | assembler memory is lower because      |\n|                   | than Pass 2                            | code sizes are comparable              |\n+-------------------+----------------------------------------+----------------------------------------+\n| Expression        | Complex for expressions like           | Extremely clean for expressions—leaves |\n| Support           | A+5 into (S, 01)+5                     | A+5 in source string form for Pass 2   |\n+-------------------+----------------------------------------+----------------------------------------+",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
