      "text": "1. Initialize:\n   LC := 0; pooltab_ptr := 1; POOLTAB[1] := 1; littab_ptr := 1;\n\n2. WHILE statement != 'END' DO:\n   a. IF label is present THEN\n         Search SYMTAB:\n            - If found with address: Flag error (Duplicate Definition).\n            - Else: Enter (label, LC) into SYMTAB.\n\n   b. IF opcode is an Assembler Directive (AD):\n         - START <addr> : LC := <addr>\n         - ORIGIN <expr>: LC := Value of <expr>\n         - EQU <expr>   : SYMTAB[label].address := Value of <expr>\n         - LTORG        : Allocate memory to unallocated literals in current pool:\n                          FOR i := POOLTAB[pooltab_ptr] TO (littab_ptr - 1) DO\n                              LITTAB[i].address := LC;  LC := LC + 1;\n                          END FOR;\n                          pooltab_ptr := pooltab_ptr + 1;\n                          POOLTAB[pooltab_ptr] := littab_ptr;\n\n   c. ELSE IF opcode is a Declaration Statement (DL):\n         - DS <size>    : LC := LC + <size>\n         - DC '<val>'   : LC := LC + 1\n\n   d. ELSE IF opcode is an Imperative Statement (IS):\n         - If operand has a Literal:\n              Enter literal into LITTAB (if not in current pool); littab_ptr := littab_ptr + 1;\n         - If operand has a Symbol:\n              Enter into SYMTAB (address blank if not declared yet);\n         - LC := LC + 1;\n\n   e. Generate Intermediate Code (IC) for the statement.\n   f. Read next statement.\n   END WHILE;\n\n3. On 'END':\n   Allocate addresses to remaining literals (identical to LTORG loop).",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Initialize:\n   LC := 0; pooltab_ptr := 1; POOLTAB[1] := 1; littab_ptr := 1;\n\n2. WHILE statement != 'END' DO:\n   a. IF label is present THEN\n         Search SYMTAB:\n            - If found with address: Flag error (Duplicate Definition).\n            - Else: Enter (label, LC) into SYMTAB.\n\n   b. IF opcode is an Assembler Directive (AD):\n         - START <addr> : LC := <addr>\n         - ORIGIN <expr>: LC := Value of <expr>\n         - EQU <expr>   : SYMTAB[label].address := Value of <expr>\n         - LTORG        : Allocate memory to unallocated literals in current pool:\n                          FOR i := POOLTAB[pooltab_ptr] TO (littab_ptr - 1) DO\n                              LITTAB[i].address := LC;  LC := LC + 1;\n                          END FOR;\n                          pooltab_ptr := pooltab_ptr + 1;\n                          POOLTAB[pooltab_ptr] := littab_ptr;\n\n   c. ELSE IF opcode is a Declaration Statement (DL):\n         - DS <size>    : LC := LC + <size>\n         - DC '<val>'   : LC := LC + 1\n\n   d. ELSE IF opcode is an Imperative Statement (IS):\n         - If operand has a Literal:\n              Enter literal into LITTAB (if not in current pool); littab_ptr := littab_ptr + 1;\n         - If operand has a Symbol:\n              Enter into SYMTAB (address blank if not declared yet);\n         - LC := LC + 1;\n\n   e. Generate Intermediate Code (IC) for the statement.\n   f. Read next statement.\n   END WHILE;\n\n3. On 'END':\n   Allocate addresses to remaining literals (identical to LTORG loop).",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "m5ixsZP-9x1yMUSSckSvI",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 8902.110501889927,
      "y": 5176.940947229919,
      "width": 1000.998779296875,
      "height": 600,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#fff4e6",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b7w",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 317474236,
      "version": 87,
      "versionNonce": 465987204,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1789621155481,
      "created": 1789621132278,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Open IC file for reading.\n\n2. WHILE statement != 'END' DO:\n   a. IF IC entry is an Imperative Statement (IS):\n         - Opcode := Extract machine opcode from IC.\n         - Register := Extract register/condition code operand.\n         - Address :=\n              - If operand is Symbol (S, index)  -> Lookup SYMTAB[index].address.\n              - If operand is Literal (L, index) -> Lookup LITTAB[index].address.\n         - Assemble and write machine instruction: <Opcode, Register, Address>.\n\n   b. ELSE IF IC entry is a Declaration Statement (DL):\n         - DC: Generate constant data word in target memory.\n         - DS: Skip/reserve specified number of memory words.\n\n   c. ELSE IF IC entry is an Assembler Directive (AD):\n         - LTORG: Emit the literal values into their allocated memory addresses.\n         - START / ORIGIN / EQU: No target code generated (internal assembler action only).\n\n   d. Read next IC entry.\n   END WHILE;\n\n3. On 'END':\n   Emit remaining literal values in target code. Close files.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Open IC file for reading.\n\n2. WHILE statement != 'END' DO:\n   a. IF IC entry is an Imperative Statement (IS):\n         - Opcode := Extract machine opcode from IC.\n         - Register := Extract register/condition code operand.\n         - Address :=\n              - If operand is Symbol (S, index)  -> Lookup SYMTAB[index].address.\n              - If operand is Literal (L, index) -> Lookup LITTAB[index].address.\n         - Assemble and write machine instruction: <Opcode, Register, Address>.\n\n   b. ELSE IF IC entry is a Declaration Statement (DL):\n         - DC: Generate constant data word in target memory.\n         - DS: Skip/reserve specified number of memory words.\n\n   c. ELSE IF IC entry is an Assembler Directive (AD):\n         - LTORG: Emit the literal values into their allocated memory addresses.\n         - START / ORIGIN / EQU: No target code generated (internal assembler action only).\n\n   d. Read next IC entry.\n   END WHILE;\n\n3. On 'END':\n   Emit remaining literal values in target code. Close files.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ZtOXGaaD8HAVwtwrQ1IvD",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 9260.616361264927,
      "y": 4092.8784472299194,
      "width": 1088.9986572265625,
      "height": 725,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#fff4e6",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b7x",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 901006596,
      "version": 116,
      "versionNonce": 1917716996,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "NEviDtcAfwpUNdh8PNlpt",
          "type": "arrow"
        },
        {
          "id": "q0dU15HBTU8JaLJvdTnn9",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1789621621267,
      "created": 1789621223066,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Initialize:\n   LC := 0; POOLTAB[1] := 1; littab_ptr := 1; pooltab_ptr := 1;\n\n2. While current statement is not 'END' do:\n   a. If a label is present:\n      - If label already exists in SYMTAB with an address, flag an error.\n      - Otherwise, add (label, LC) to SYMTAB.\n\n   b. If instruction is an Assembler Directive (AD):\n      - START / ORIGIN: Update LC to the given address.\n      - EQU: Set SYMTAB[label].address := evaluated address.\n      - LTORG: For each unallocated literal in LITTAB for the current pool,\n               assign its address := LC and increment LC := LC + 1.\n               Increment pooltab_ptr and set POOLTAB[pooltab_ptr] := littab_ptr.\n\n   c. Else if instruction is a Declaration Statement (DL):\n      - DS: Increment LC := LC + size.\n      - DC: Increment LC := LC + 1.\n\n   d. Else if instruction is an Imperative Statement (IS):\n      - If operand has a new literal, add it to LITTAB; littab_ptr := littab_ptr + 1.\n      - If operand has a new symbol, add it to SYMTAB.\n      - Increment LC := LC + 1.\n\n   e. Generate Intermediate Code (IC) for this statement.\n   f. Read next statement.\n\n3. On 'END':\n   Assign memory addresses to all remaining literals in LITTAB starting at LC (same as LTORG loop).",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Initialize:\n   LC := 0; POOLTAB[1] := 1; littab_ptr := 1; pooltab_ptr := 1;\n\n2. While current statement is not 'END' do:\n   a. If a label is present:\n      - If label already exists in SYMTAB with an address, flag an error.\n      - Otherwise, add (label, LC) to SYMTAB.\n\n   b. If instruction is an Assembler Directive (AD):\n      - START / ORIGIN: Update LC to the given address.\n      - EQU: Set SYMTAB[label].address := evaluated address.\n      - LTORG: For each unallocated literal in LITTAB for the current pool,\n               assign its address := LC and increment LC := LC + 1.\n               Increment pooltab_ptr and set POOLTAB[pooltab_ptr] := littab_ptr.\n\n   c. Else if instruction is a Declaration Statement (DL):\n      - DS: Increment LC := LC + size.\n      - DC: Increment LC := LC + 1.\n\n   d. Else if instruction is an Imperative Statement (IS):\n      - If operand has a new literal, add it to LITTAB; littab_ptr := littab_ptr + 1.\n      - If operand has a new symbol, add it to SYMTAB.\n      - Increment LC := LC + 1.\n\n   e. Generate Intermediate Code (IC) for this statement.\n   f. Read next statement.\n\n3. On 'END':\n   Assign memory addresses to all remaining literals in LITTAB starting at LC (same as LTORG loop).",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "_UZ1BR7-lJ7uAdvIav-LK",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 9347.941231056593,
      "y": 4913.805530563253,
      "width": 1000.9986572265625,
      "height": 575,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#fff4e6",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b7y",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 743375292,
      "version": 273,
      "versionNonce": 1863046660,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "k5xmnBYmFonA60SQ77mbO",
          "type": "arrow"
        },
        {
          "id": "q0dU15HBTU8JaLJvdTnn9",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1789621938667,
      "created": 1789621229437,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Open the Intermediate Code (IC) file and point to the start.\n\n2. While current IC entry is not 'END' do:\n   a. If entry is an Imperative Statement (IS):\n      - Get the machine opcode from OPTAB.\n      - Get the register or condition code.\n      - For memory operand:\n        * If symbol: Look up address in SYMTAB.\n        * If literal: Look up address in LITTAB.\n      - Assemble and write the final machine instruction: <Opcode, Reg, Address>.\n\n   b. Else if entry is a Declaration Statement (DL):\n      - DC: Emit the constant value into memory.\n      - DS: Reserve the specified number of memory words (no code generated).\n\n   c. Else if entry is an Assembler Directive (AD):\n      - LTORG: Emit binary values of all literals in the pool at their allocated addresses.\n      - START / ORIGIN / EQU: No target code generated.\n\n   d. Read next IC entry.\n\n3. On 'END':\n   Emit the values of any remaining literals into their memory locations; close files.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Open the Intermediate Code (IC) file and point to the start.\n\n2. While current IC entry is not 'END' do:\n   a. If entry is an Imperative Statement (IS):\n      - Get the machine opcode from OPTAB.\n      - Get the register or condition code.\n      - For memory operand:\n        * If symbol: Look up address in SYMTAB.\n        * If literal: Look up address in LITTAB.\n      - Assemble and write the final machine instruction: <Opcode, Reg, Address>.\n\n   b. Else if entry is a Declaration Statement (DL):\n      - DC: Emit the constant value into memory.\n      - DS: Reserve the specified number of memory words (no code generated).\n\n   c. Else if entry is an Assembler Directive (AD):\n      - LTORG: Emit binary values of all literals in the pool at their allocated addresses.\n      - START / ORIGIN / EQU: No target code generated.\n\n   d. Read next IC entry.\n\n3. On 'END':\n   Emit the values of any remaining literals into their memory locations; close files.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "p35nzSbYxMXQMYX2Jwarc",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 8108.575345639927,
      "y": 4159.577665979919,
      "width": 978.9987182617188,
      "height": 725,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#fff4e6",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b7z",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 414207748,
      "version": 65,
      "versionNonce": 424275076,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "QEHDA1TEV9vhuoZbBXS7Z",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1789621647214,
      "created": 1789621235498,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Initialize:\n   LC := 0;\n\n2. While current statement is not 'END' do:\n   a. If a label is present:\n      - If already defined in SYMTAB, flag duplicate definition error.\n      - If symbol exists but is unresolved:\n        * Set SYMTAB[label].address := LC and mark it as DEFINED.\n        * Backpatch: Walk the TII (Table of Incomplete Instructions) chain for this\n          symbol and write LC into every instruction that referenced it.\n      - If new, add (label, LC, DEFINED) to SYMTAB.\n\n   b. If instruction is an Imperative Statement (IS):\n      - Look up opcode and register.\n      - For memory symbol:\n        * If defined in SYMTAB: Use its known address.\n        * If forward reference (undefined/unseen):\n          Put 0 (blank) in the address field.\n          Add current LC to the symbol's chain in TII.\n          If symbol is not in SYMTAB, add it as UNDEFINED.\n      - Emit machine code directly to memory at LC.\n      - Increment LC := LC + 1.\n\n   c. If instruction is DL or AD:\n      - Update LC accordingly (DS / DC / ORIGIN).\n      - LTORG / END: Assign addresses to pending literals, emit their values immediately,\n        and backpatch instructions referencing them.\n\n   d. Read next statement.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Initialize:\n   LC := 0;\n\n2. While current statement is not 'END' do:\n   a. If a label is present:\n      - If already defined in SYMTAB, flag duplicate definition error.\n      - If symbol exists but is unresolved:\n        * Set SYMTAB[label].address := LC and mark it as DEFINED.\n        * Backpatch: Walk the TII (Table of Incomplete Instructions) chain for this\n          symbol and write LC into every instruction that referenced it.\n      - If new, add (label, LC, DEFINED) to SYMTAB.\n\n   b. If instruction is an Imperative Statement (IS):\n      - Look up opcode and register.\n      - For memory symbol:\n        * If defined in SYMTAB: Use its known address.\n        * If forward reference (undefined/unseen):\n          Put 0 (blank) in the address field.\n          Add current LC to the symbol's chain in TII.\n          If symbol is not in SYMTAB, add it as UNDEFINED.\n      - Emit machine code directly to memory at LC.\n      - Increment LC := LC + 1.\n\n   c. If instruction is DL or AD:\n      - Update LC accordingly (DS / DC / ORIGIN).\n      - LTORG / END: Assign addresses to pending literals, emit their values immediately,\n        and backpatch instructions referencing them.\n\n   d. Read next statement.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "RYk_pNh9Xbw0K2jIXorCu",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10601.19126205858,
      "y": 2757.3135910791243,
      "width": 780.9989624023438,
      "height": 1725,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#6741d9",
      "backgroundColor": "#fff4e6",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b80",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1164707460,
      "version": 204,
      "versionNonce": 1180554116,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "NEviDtcAfwpUNdh8PNlpt",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1789621681112,
      "created": 1789621396535,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. INITIALIZATION:\n   LC := 0;\n   pooltab_ptr := 1;\n   POOLTAB[1] := 1;\n   littab_ptr := 1;\n\n2. STATEMENT PROCESSING LOOP:\n   WHILE next statement is NOT 'END' DO:\n   \n     a. Process Label:\n        IF statement has a Label THEN\n            this_label := Symbol in label field;\n            Enter (this_label, LC) into SYMTAB;\n        END IF;\n\n     b. Process LTORG Directive:\n        IF statement is 'LTORG' THEN\n            -- Allocate memory for unallocated literals in current pool\n            FOR i := POOLTAB[pooltab_ptr] TO (littab_ptr - 1) DO:\n                LITTAB[i].address := LC;\n                LC := LC + 1;\n            END FOR;\n            pooltab_ptr := pooltab_ptr + 1;\n            POOLTAB[pooltab_ptr] := littab_ptr;\n        END IF;\n\n     c. Process START or ORIGIN Directive:\n        IF statement is 'START' or 'ORIGIN' THEN\n            LC := Evaluated value of operand field;\n        END IF;\n\n     d. Process EQU Directive:\n        IF statement is 'EQU' THEN\n            this_addr := Evaluated value of <address spec>;\n            Update SYMTAB entry for this_label to address = this_addr;\n        END IF;\n\n     e. Process Declaration Statements (DS / DC):\n        IF statement is 'DS' or 'DC' THEN\n            code := Statement opcode ('01' for DC, '02' for DS);\n            size := Memory size required;\n            Generate IC: '(DL, code) (C, constant_val)';\n            LC := LC + size;\n        END IF;\n\n     f. Process Imperative Statements (IS):\n        IF statement is an Imperative Instruction THEN\n            code := Machine Opcode from OPTAB;\n            length := Instruction length from OPTAB;\n            \n            -- Handle Operand\n            IF operand is a Literal ('=val') THEN\n                LITTAB[littab_ptr] := '=val';\n                this_literal_no := littab_ptr;\n                littab_ptr := littab_ptr + 1;\n                Generate IC: '(IS, code) (reg) (L, this_literal_no)';\n            ELSE (operand is a Symbol)\n                this_entry := SYMTAB entry number of symbol;\n                Generate IC: '(IS, code) (reg) (S, this_entry)';\n            END IF;\n            \n            LC := LC + length;\n        END IF;\n   END WHILE;\n\n3. END STATEMENT PROCESSING:\n   a. Process remaining literals in LITTAB (same as LTORG step 2b).\n   b. Generate IC: '(AD, 02)' for END.\n   c. Pass control to Pass 2.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. INITIALIZATION:\n   LC := 0;\n   pooltab_ptr := 1;\n   POOLTAB[1] := 1;\n   littab_ptr := 1;\n\n2. STATEMENT PROCESSING LOOP:\n   WHILE next statement is NOT 'END' DO:\n   \n     a. Process Label:\n        IF statement has a Label THEN\n            this_label := Symbol in label field;\n            Enter (this_label, LC) into SYMTAB;\n        END IF;\n\n     b. Process LTORG Directive:\n        IF statement is 'LTORG' THEN\n            -- Allocate memory for unallocated literals in current pool\n            FOR i := POOLTAB[pooltab_ptr] TO (littab_ptr - 1) DO:\n                LITTAB[i].address := LC;\n                LC := LC + 1;\n            END FOR;\n            pooltab_ptr := pooltab_ptr + 1;\n            POOLTAB[pooltab_ptr] := littab_ptr;\n        END IF;\n\n     c. Process START or ORIGIN Directive:\n        IF statement is 'START' or 'ORIGIN' THEN\n            LC := Evaluated value of operand field;\n        END IF;\n\n     d. Process EQU Directive:\n        IF statement is 'EQU' THEN\n            this_addr := Evaluated value of <address spec>;\n            Update SYMTAB entry for this_label to address = this_addr;\n        END IF;\n\n     e. Process Declaration Statements (DS / DC):\n        IF statement is 'DS' or 'DC' THEN\n            code := Statement opcode ('01' for DC, '02' for DS);\n            size := Memory size required;\n            Generate IC: '(DL, code) (C, constant_val)';\n            LC := LC + size;\n        END IF;\n\n     f. Process Imperative Statements (IS):\n        IF statement is an Imperative Instruction THEN\n            code := Machine Opcode from OPTAB;\n            length := Instruction length from OPTAB;\n            \n            -- Handle Operand\n            IF operand is a Literal ('=val') THEN\n                LITTAB[littab_ptr] := '=val';\n                this_literal_no := littab_ptr;\n                littab_ptr := littab_ptr + 1;\n                Generate IC: '(IS, code) (reg) (L, this_literal_no)';\n            ELSE (operand is a Symbol)\n                this_entry := SYMTAB entry number of symbol;\n                Generate IC: '(IS, code) (reg) (S, this_entry)';\n            END IF;\n            \n            LC := LC + length;\n        END IF;\n   END WHILE;\n\n3. END STATEMENT PROCESSING:\n   a. Process remaining literals in LITTAB (same as LTORG step 2b).\n   b. Generate IC: '(AD, 02)' for END.\n   c. Pass control to Pass 2.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
